  "text": "[[378.12]] <b>49 Zum Traité de physique von Jacques Rohault </b> <span>378.12;0:62:049:7105-7110:L:l^</span>.\n[[378.13]] Sustentaculum nubium, etsi graves factae sint[,] latitudo. Etiam saxum latum et\n[[378.13]] semper horizonti parallelum difficilius descendet in aëre quam horizonti perpendiculare.\n[[378.14]] Conatur enim si liberum sit convertere sese in eum statum quo sit perpendiculare, uti\n[[378.15]] contra lignum aquae innatans in statum parallelum. Imminuitur ergo gravitas, quia\n[[379.1]] difficilius aqua finditur, et potest latitudo esse evecta ut saxum. Praesertim si paulum aëri\n[[379.2]] inter ipsum et aquam interceptum sit, ut si sit paulum concavum omnino supernatet\n[[379.3]] Idem in aëre de nubibus. Ut magnes ita et grave habet quandam directionem seu vertici\n[[379.4]] tatem, tum ad perpendicularem, tum a perpendiculari.\n[[379.5]] An aër necessarius sit imbuendo igni an replendo loco fumi abeuntis, ita disci potes\n[[379.6]] experimento. Cave ne fumus exeat, at auctus extinguet ignem, fac ergo absorberi in locun\n[[379.7]] unde aër sit exhaustus. Si ignis ideo tantum traheret, ut fumi locus suppleretur[,] noi\n[[379.8]] augeretur ignis proportione aucti foraminis.\n[[379.9]] Rohault. p. 1. cap. 9. Phys. de possibili dilatatione auri. Adde ei Tincturam aqua\n[[379.10]] per Cochinelium Boylii de coloribus 5 lignes  ^#'1/7  divisae in 65159) partes aequales\n[[379.11]] Boylii tinctura 125000 vicibus latius extensa. Massae aequales et ut 19 ad 1 pondere\n[[379.12]] Nota circulationem motuum ubique esse ut in mentem venit ex Rohault. p. 1. c. 12\n[[379.13]] Qualis est magnetica de qua ille lib. 3. cap. 8. de magnete. Mihi videtur ignis fere agere\n[[379.14]] et trahere ut magnes.\n[[379.15]] Nota: potest dici Lacrymam instar ignis circumsilire.\n[[379.16]] In privilegio regio praeter morem laudes continentur: nostre cher et bien aimé Jacques\n[[379.17]] Rohault s'estant toute sa vie appliqué à l'estude de la philosophie et des mathematiques a\n[[379.18]] composé plusieurs traitez, entre autres un traité de Physique ou de la science naturelle;et celuy de\n[[379.19]] Cosmographie veus par le S de Meseray nostre Cons et Historiographe; les 15 livres de\n[[379.20]] Elemens d'Euclide, l'Arithmetique practique, la resolution des Triangles rectilignes et\n[[379.21]] spheriques, la geometrie practique,r les fortifications les mechaniques et la perspectiver à ces causes\n[[379.22]] voulant donner au dit Sieur Rohault des marques de l'estime particuliere que nous faisons\n[[379.23]] de sa personne pour l'exciter à continuer ses recherches\n[[379.24]] Rohault. Phys. part. 1. cap. 12. machinam invenit qua per experientiam ostendi\n[[379.25]] potest totum descensurum esse argentum vivum, si contra nullus aër crassus ponderare\n[[379.26]] Quod tamen prima fronte videri queat non posse effici quam\n[[379.27]] extra aërem nostrum. Hoc destruit funiculum.\n[[379.28]] cap. 14. n. 9. eandem determinationem motuum ex pluribus\n[[379.29]] compositam esse quia eadem recta diversorum\n[[379.30]] rectangulorum diagonalis esse potest, sed putat non necessarium\n[[379.31]] considerare omnes, ego contra.\n[[380.1]] Rohault. p. 1. Phys. cap. 24. philosophatur non ineleganter de sapore insipido, acido,\n[[380.2]] dulci, amaro. Insipidum figurarum esse quae non vellicant ut rotundarum, acidas pungere,\n[[380.3]] dulces titillare seu subtilius pungere, amaras esse nimis dulces, ac proinde molestas.\n[[380.4]] Rohault. Phys. lib. 1. cap. 31. n. 2). putat nervorum duorum opticorum filamenta\n[[380.5]] esse aequalia tandemque duo quaelibet filamenta sibi correspondentia uniri non ineleganter.\n[[380.6]] ( Videndum an hoc conciliabile cum experimento Boylii cui oculus alter impressam solis\n[[380.7]] imaginem depravatam habuit, alter non habuit. )\n[[380.8]] cap. ult. explicat observationem radiorum imaginariorum e lucidis exeuntium si oculo\n[[380.9]] contracto videntur, de quibus non memini tractatum esse. Addere potuisset eos qui oculo\n[[380.10]] elevato videntur.\n[[380.11]] part. 2. cap. 27. Astrologia judiciaria orta est quod Sapientes Aegyptii notassent\n[[380.12]] dies diversitate siderum quae immediate post occasum solis surgunt, et populum eodem\n[[380.13]] tempore de tempestate statu aëris regulis agriculturae monuissent. Factum est, ut signum\n[[380.14]] habitum sit pro causa. n. 16. Cancri seu Gammari nec vacui nec pleni sunt pro lunae\n[[380.15]] ratione, idem de ostreis.\n[[380.16]] part. 3. c. 2. n. 5. 6. 7. descriptio fontis artificialis portabilis ope aëris compressi,\n[[380.17]] instar sclopeti ventanei, sed ut rei minime rarae. cap. 4. eleganter satis explicat naturam\n[[380.18]] salis foliolis quibusdam aut saltem aciculis volitantibus et se componentibus. Crepitationem\n[[380.19]] salis esse ab aqua inclusa.\n[[380.20]] Cap. 8. eleganter admodum tractat de magnete, et experimentis a Cartesio non\n[[380.21]] tactis applicat. Praeter modum dandi baculis chalybeis vim magneticam in momento,\n[[380.22]] illustrat eleganter etiam circulationes suas materiae hinc exeuntis hinc redeuntis visibili\n[[380.23]] limaturae feri dispositione super chartam cui suppositus magnes, et ostendit variationes,\n[[380.24]] si lapidi cuidam non insint nisi quaedam venae magneticae. ( Unde haberi potest modus\n[[380.25]] probandi interiorem magnetis constitutionem. )\n[[380.26]] Rohaultius experimentum fecit: baculi ferrei in aqua situ ad horizontem\n[[380.27]] perpendiculari extincti, inde enim magnetismus ferro. Cum diuturnus situs talis eundem\n[[380.28]] magnetismum ferro tribuat. Ait Hobbes de corpore etiam ferum si diu in plano meridiani\n[[380.29]] quieverit, etiam dimotum ad id reversurum. Tentandum ergo an ferrum acquirat vim\n[[381.1]] magneticam, si extinguatur in situ meridianae lineae congruente. Et an utroque casu tum\n[[381.2]] Rohaultiano tum nostro absit declinatio; et perveniri possit ad Meridianum universalem commodius\n[[381.3]] quam tentamento Grandamici. Omnia corpora contigua sunt continua. Demonstrabitur a\n[[381.4]] me quia omne corpus movetur, et quicquid movetur conatur in omnes plagas. Omne\n[[381.5]] corpus moveri demonstro, quia datur vacuum. Vacuum habet magnitudinem figuram.\n[[381.6]] Corpori ergo aliud quiddam tribuendum est. Nihil aliud autem ei tribui potest, quam\n[[381.7]] magnitudinis et figurae seu spatii mutatio, id est motus. Dari vacuum ostendo quia alioquin\n[[381.8]] non dabuntur motus eccentrici. Dari motus Eccentricos constat, alioquin nulla esset\n[[381.9]] varietas in Mundo.\n[[381.10]] Ratio quam Cartesius affert cur radii in corporibus durioribus refringantur ad\n[[381.11]] perpendicularem non satisfacit. Vera haec est, quod corpus in quo plus aetheris magis luminis\n[[381.12]] detorsioni resistit, turbaretur enim. Magis ergo turbari potest in quo aetheris minus, et\n[[381.13]] unde aether motus sui detorsionem majore consequentia sentit. Solem magis per motum\n[[381.14]] agere quam lumen intelligas, quia sole maculis obducto aut eclipsato nulla notabilis mutatio\n[[381.15]] in Mundo.\n[[381.16]] Rohault methodum hanc tenet, ut enumeratis experimentis principalibus, ex his\n[[381.17]] hypothesin, et ex hypothesi caetera deducat. Ut apparet in Magnete differentia inter\n[[381.18]] methodum eius et Cartesianam.\n",
  "number": "49",
  "title": "Zum Traité de physique von Jacques Rohault",
  "date": ""
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:49 Zum Traité de physique von Jacques Rohault 378.12;0:62:049:7105-7110:L:l^. Sustentaculum nubium, etsi graves factae sint[,] latitudo. Etiam saxum latum et semper horizonti parallelum difficilius descendet in aëre quam horizonti perpendiculare. Conatur enim si liberum sit convertere sese in eum st...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>